notes:
Closed 2026-05-28 as deferred operational task — does NOT block .16 writer replacement on a fresh catalog. The orphan owner 1.22 qmrr-zm2n is on Hal's local catalog only (RDR-137 §Research Findings A4). Manual remediation (when Hal chooses):

  sqlite3 ~/.config/nexus/catalog/.catalog.db <<EOF
    -- Verify the orphan
    SELECT tumbler_prefix, name, repo_root FROM owners WHERE tumbler_prefix = '1.22';
    -- Re-point any documents bound to 1.22 at 1.1 (canonical nexus owner)
    UPDATE documents SET tumbler = REPLACE(tumbler, '1.22.', '1.1.') WHERE tumbler LIKE '1.22.%';
    -- Drop the orphan owner row
    DELETE FROM owners WHERE tumbler_prefix = '1.22';
EOF

A generic 'nx catalog cleanup-orphan-owners' verb is a worthwhile P3 follow-on (file separately when needed); the live data point is single and easily fixed by hand. .16's semantic dependency on .15 (per audit) applies to systems with multiple orphan owners — not the case here, so .16 can proceed standalone.

